.th MESSAGE VI 1/1/76
.sh NAME
message \*- print a message in large letters
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd Message
.br
(lines of text)
.br
(seperated by new lines)
.br
(eleven chars per line)
.br
(five lines per page)
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Message
constructs a message on standard output, using
a large character set (each of size 12 x 12 chars.).
Font size allows five lines per page, eleven characters per line.
.s3
A <NEW PAGE> prompt begins the message, and all subsequent
new pages.
.sh FILES
.nf
.if t .ta 1.2i
.if n .ta 14
/etc/letters	large letters
.fi
.dt
.sh AUTHOR
Keith Titmuss (University of New South Wales)
.sh BUGS
